OpenOCD Third-Party Support
===========================

This repository is a FORK of OpenOCD (upstream: https://github.com/openocd-org/openocd).

It is a complete, buildable OpenOCD source tree. The difference from upstream is
that it additionally carries chip, board and probe support that lives only in
third-party OpenOCD forks and has never been accepted upstream.

    Upstream tree            : openocd-org/openocd, GPL-2.0-or-later
    Third-party additions    : imported from 53 public forks, 546 files
    Layout                   : identical to upstream (in-tree, no overlay)

The layout is deliberately identical to upstream so that the fork can be
updated with a plain merge and so that a file can be traced back to its
origin without a mapping table:

    git fetch upstream
    git merge upstream/master

Every imported file is recorded in manifest/PROVENANCE.json together with the
source repository, branch, commit and SHA-256 digest it was taken from.

LICENCE
------

The OpenOCD source code in this tree is provided under the terms of the GNU
General Public License version 2 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later), as provided in
LICENSES/preferred/GPL-2.0. The OpenOCD documentation is provided under the
terms of the GNU Free Documentation License version 1.2 or later without
Invariant Sections (GFDL-1.2-no-invariants-or-later). See COPYING and
LICENSES/license-rules.txt for the full statement and the per-file rules.

The third-party files added by this fork are NOT covered by that blanket
statement, and no single licence applies to the whole repository:

  * Most forks inherit GPL-2.0-or-later from upstream, but only 139 of the
    546 imported files carry a licence field that GitHub could resolve as
    GPL-2.0.
  * 382 files record NOASSERTION. That means "GitHub could not determine the
    terms" - it does NOT mean the terms are permissive. Some of these files
    carry proprietary notices, for example the flash algorithms in
    analogdevicesinc/openocd, which state "This software is proprietary to
    Analog Devices, Inc."
  * 25 files carry no licence information at all.

BEFORE ANY COMMERCIAL USE you must audit the licence header of every file you
intend to redistribute. The machine-readable index is:

    manifest/licenses.csv       every imported file -> repo / branch /
                                 commit / licence
    docs/03-LICENSES.md         human-readable version of the same data
    manifest/PROVENANCE.json    authoritative provenance for all 546 files
    manifest/tier1-PROVENANCE.json
    manifest/tier2-PROVENANCE.json
                                 the same data, split by import layer

Files that were imported and then deliberately removed from this fork are
listed with the reason in the "removed_from_tree" section of the provenance
manifests, so the audit trail is complete in both directions.

This fork is distributed WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY, to the extent permitted by law.
